{
  "$comment": [
    "Recto's icons (ADR-0027 §2.6–§2.8; components/09-primitives.md §30; language.md §5).",
    "`icons` maps each app name to its Phosphor source: the same name unless `from` says otherwise.",
    "`fill: true` also takes the fill twin, for glyphs that show a selected state (the armed tool,",
    "the current tab or segment, an on toggle; I-2). Action glyphs (close, plus, check, carets,",
    "arrows, more) never swap, so they carry no twin. The three slots named for a concept (redact,",
    "edit-text, compare) point at Phosphor fallbacks until their custom glyphs land (I-7).",
    "`lucide` is the migration table of D3-6: every Lucide name the app imported before, with the",
    "app name it became. An array lists the default first, then the names used where the same",
    "Lucide glyph meant something else (`context` says where). `pnpm icons` fails on any name",
    "that is not in @phosphor-icons/core, on a missing fill twin and on a table entry that",
    "points at no icon."
  ],
